IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cea-elector`

-- Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918 (Cth) -- the candidate: who is qualified to be elected and capable of being nominated
-- (ss 163, 164, 165), the nomination, the qualification checklist and the deadline (ss 166, 170, 172, 175), the $2,000 deposit
-- and its return at 4% (ss 170(2)(b), 173), election funding for an unendorsed candidate (s 294), when a person is a candidate
-- for Part XX (s 287(9)), the candidate's own agent (s 289(2)), and the candidate return (s 310A).
--
-- SEAT: the candidate -- the elector who stands for the Senate or the House of Representatives (Daniel, in 2040). Every
-- decision is phrased as that person would ask it ("May I stand", "Is my nomination valid", "Do I get my deposit back", "Must I
-- lodge a candidate return"). Section 44 of the Constitution is a separate subject: whether I am incapable of being chosen
-- under it is a BORROWED FACT, asked, never worked out here.
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 81, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 16, 2025 (register id
-- C2026C00260, in 2 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1918A00027.txt. The Commonwealth Electoral
-- Regulation 2016 is not deposited; Form DB (the qualification checklist, alterable by regulations under s 392) is not
-- transcribed, and answering "every mandatory question" in it is a fact. The s 294 dollar figures are indexed under s 321 from
-- the Australian Statistician's CPI, which is not deposited: the rate per vote and the threshold are INPUTS. The value of a
-- penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA) is an INPUT.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Senate group requests (s 168) beyond the deposit test; bulk nominations (s 170(2)(a)(i)) beyond their 48-hour
-- deadline; sitting independents' single signature (s 166(1C)-(1E)); formal-defect leniency (s 172(2)) beyond its exclusion of
-- the checklist and the renunciation documents; withdrawal and death of candidates (ss 177, 180); party endorsement and
-- registration (Part XI); election funding for groups and parties (ss 293, 295), its claims and payment (ss 297-299); gift caps
-- and expenditure caps (Divisions 3A, 3AB); expedited disclosure and federal accounts; the contents of the return beyond
-- whether it is due; the Court of Disputed Returns (Part XXII).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Commonwealth Electoral Act 1918 -- the candidate`

DECLARE `My standing` HAS
    `I am a member of a State Parliament or a Territory Legislative Assembly at the hour of nomination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am incapable of being chosen under section 44 of the Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am nominated for another election on the same polling day at the hour of nomination` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `163, 164, 165 -- who may stand`

-- s 163(1): a person who "(a) has reached the age of 18 years; (b) is an Australian citizen; and (c) is either: (i) an elector
-- entitled to vote at a House of Representatives election; or (ii) a person qualified to become such an elector; is qualified
-- to be elected". (2): a person "is not entitled to be nominated ... unless the person is qualified under subsection (1)".
-- Paragraph (c)(ii) is read as entitled to enrolment (s 93(1)), which the s 93(8AA) prisoner keeps.
@export Am I qualified to be elected as a Senator or a Member of the House of Representatives (s 163(1))?
GIVEN `me`      IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances as an elector
      `the day` IS A DATE               @desc The day of nomination, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I qualified to be elected` IF
        `Have I reached the age` `me` 18 `the day`
    AND `me`'s `I am an Australian citizen`
    AND (    `Am I entitled to vote at the election` `me` `the day`
         OR  `Am I entitled to enrolment` `me` `the day`)

-- s 164: a person who is, "at the hour of nomination, a member of: (a) the Parliament of a State; (b) the Legislative Assembly of
-- the Northern Territory of Australia; or (c) the Legislative Assembly for the Australian Capital Territory; is not capable of
-- being nominated". s 165(1): where nominations of a person exist "for 2 or more" elections on the same polling day at the hour
-- of nomination, "each of those nominations is invalid".
@export Am I capable of being nominated, as far as this Act goes (ss 163(2), 164, 165)?
GIVEN `me`       IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances as an elector
      `standing` IS A `My standing`      @desc Your other offices and nominations, and your answer on section 44 of the Constitution
      `the day`  IS A DATE               @desc The day of nomination, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I capable of being nominated` IF
        `Am I qualified to be elected` `me` `the day`
    AND NOT `standing`'s `I am a member of a State Parliament or a Territory Legislative Assembly at the hour of nomination`
    AND NOT `standing`'s `I am nominated for another election on the same polling day at the hour of nomination`

-- Section 44 of the Constitution (a dual citizen, among others, "shall be incapable of being chosen") is not in this Act. It is
-- asked as a borrowed fact; this encoding does not decide it.
@export May I stand for election, as far as this Act and my answer on section 44 of the Constitution go?
GIVEN `me`       IS A `My circumstances` @desc Your circumstances as an elector
      `standing` IS A `My standing`      @desc Your other offices and nominations, and your answer on section 44 of the Constitution
      `the day`  IS A DATE               @desc The day of nomination, ISO 8601
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I stand` IF
        `Am I capable of being nominated` `me` `standing` `the day`
    AND NOT `standing`'s `I am incapable of being chosen under section 44 of the Constitution`

§§ `166, 170, 172 -- the nomination and the qualification checklist`

DECLARE `My nomination` HAS
    `it sets out my name, place of residence and occupation`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is signed by at least 100 electors entitled to vote at the election` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is signed by the registered officer of the party that endorsed me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in it I consent to act if elected`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `in it I declare I am qualified and not a candidate in another election that day` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in it I state how I am an Australian citizen, with the particulars`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `in it I answer every mandatory question in the qualification checklist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I contend that I have renounced or lost another citizenship`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `I give documents supporting that contention with the nomination`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is received after the writ and before the hour of nomination`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `my deposit of $2,000 is given before the hour of nomination`        IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 166(1): a nomination "must: (a) set out the name, place of residence and occupation of the candidate; and (b) be signed by:
-- (i) not less than 100 electors entitled to vote at the election ...; or (ii) the registered officer of the registered
-- political party by which the candidate has been endorsed". s 170(1): not valid unless the person "(a) consents to act if
-- elected; and (b) declares" qualification under the Constitution and the laws of the Commonwealth and no other candidacy that
-- day; "(c) states whether the person is an Australian citizen by reason of birth in Australia or other means" with particulars;
-- "(d) answers every mandatory question in the qualification checklist set out in Form DB". (1A): validity "is not affected if
-- an answer ... is incorrect, false or inadequate". (1B): a person who contends a foreign citizenship was renounced or lost
-- must provide supporting documents "together with the nomination". (2): received "after the issue of the writ and before"
-- the hour of nomination, with "a deposit of $2,000" given before that time. s 165(1): a double nomination is invalid.
@export Is my nomination valid (ss 165, 166(1), 170)?
GIVEN `nomination` IS A `My nomination` @desc What your nomination contains and when it and the deposit were received
      `standing`   IS A `My standing`   @desc Your other offices and nominations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my nomination valid` IF
        `nomination`'s `it sets out my name, place of residence and occupation`
    AND (    `nomination`'s `it is signed by at least 100 electors entitled to vote at the election`
         OR  `nomination`'s `it is signed by the registered officer of the party that endorsed me`)
    AND `nomination`'s `in it I consent to act if elected`
    AND `nomination`'s `in it I declare I am qualified and not a candidate in another election that day`
    AND `nomination`'s `in it I state how I am an Australian citizen, with the particulars`
    AND `nomination`'s `in it I answer every mandatory question in the qualification checklist`
    AND (    NOT `nomination`'s `I contend that I have renounced or lost another citizenship`
         OR  `nomination`'s `I give documents supporting that contention with the nomination`)
    AND `nomination`'s `it is received after the writ and before the hour of nomination`
    AND `nomination`'s `my deposit of $2,000 is given before the hour of nomination`
    AND NOT `standing`'s `I am nominated for another election on the same polling day at the hour of nomination`

-- s 172(1): "a nomination shall be rejected by the Electoral Commissioner if, and only if, the provisions of section 166, 167,
-- 170 or 171 have not been complied with". s 170A(3): the Commissioner has "no power to determine whether" a checklist answer is
-- false or a person is qualified. So the question turns on the nomination alone, never on s 163 or s 44: eligibility is for the
-- Court of Disputed Returns. Formal-defect leniency (s 172(2)) is not modelled; its note says it never saves a missing checklist
-- answer or missing renunciation documents. s 165 invalidity is not a s 172 ground and is left out here.
@export Must the Electoral Commissioner reject my nomination (s 172(1))?
GIVEN `nomination` IS A `My nomination` @desc What your nomination contains and when it and the deposit were received
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commissioner reject my nomination` IF
    NOT `Is my nomination valid` `nomination` (`My standing` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)

-- s 170(2)(b): "a deposit of $2,000". Section 321 does not list it, so it is not indexed.
@export How much is the deposit I must give with my nomination (s 170(2)(b)), in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is the deposit` IS 2000

-- s 175(1): "The hour of nomination shall be 12 o'clock noon on the day of nomination." s 170(2)(a): a bulk nomination must be
-- received "48 hours before the hour of nomination"; otherwise before the hour of nomination.
@export How many hours before noon on the day of nomination must my nomination be received (ss 170(2)(a), 175(1))?
GIVEN `it is a bulk nomination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a party's registered officer is lodging it as one of a bulk nomination
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many hours before the hour of nomination must it be received` IS
    IF `it is a bulk nomination` THEN 48 ELSE 0

§§ `173 -- return or forfeiture of the deposit`

DECLARE `The election` IS ONE OF `a House of Representatives election`, `a Senate election`

-- s 173(1): the deposit is returned "if the candidate is elected, or: (a) in the case of a Senate election: (i) if the total
-- number of votes polled in the candidate's favour as first preferences is at least 4% of the total number of votes polled in
-- favour of the candidates in the election as first preferences; or (ii)" for a candidate in a group (s 168), if the group's
-- first preferences together are at least 4%; "(b) in the case of a House of Representatives election", the candidate's own 4%;
-- "otherwise it shall be forfeited to the Commonwealth". (2): it is returned "to the person who paid it".
@export Do I get my deposit back (s 173)?
GIVEN `the election`                   IS A `The election` @desc A House of Representatives election or a Senate election
      `I was elected`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were elected
      `my first preference votes`      IS A NUMBER  @desc The first preference votes polled for you
      `I am in a Senate group`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your name was in a group on the Senate ballot paper (s 168)
      `my group's first preference votes` IS A NUMBER @desc The first preference votes polled for all the candidates in your group together (0 if none)
      `all first preference votes`     IS A NUMBER  @desc The first preference votes polled for all the candidates in the election
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I get my deposit back` IF
        `I was elected`
    OR  `at least 4%` `my first preference votes` `all first preference votes`
    OR  (    `the election` EQUALS `a Senate election`
         AND `I am in a Senate group`
         AND `at least 4%` `my group's first preference votes` `all first preference votes`)
    WHERE
        GIVEN `votes` IS A NUMBER
              `total` IS A NUMBER
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        `at least 4%` MEANS `votes` TIMES 100 AT LEAST `total` TIMES 4

§§ `294 -- election funding for an unendorsed candidate`

-- s 294(1): payable if the candidate is "neither: (i) endorsed by a registered political party; nor (ii) in the case of a
-- Senate election--a member of a group; and (b) the total number of formal first preference votes given for the candidate ...
-- is at least 4% of the total number of formal first preference votes cast".
@export Is election funding payable for me as a candidate no party endorsed (s 294(1))?
GIVEN `the election`                   IS A `The election` @desc A House of Representatives election or a Senate election
      `I am endorsed by a registered party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a registered political party endorsed you
      `I am in a Senate group`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a member of a group in a Senate election
      `my formal first preference votes` IS A NUMBER @desc The formal first preference votes given for you
      `all formal first preference votes` IS A NUMBER @desc The formal first preference votes cast in the election
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is election funding payable for me` IF
        NOT `I am endorsed by a registered party`
    AND NOT (`the election` EQUALS `a Senate election` AND `I am in a Senate group`)
    AND `my formal first preference votes` TIMES 100 AT LEAST `all formal first preference votes` TIMES 4

-- s 294(2): "(a) the amount worked out by multiplying $5 by the number of formal first preference votes ...; or (b) if the amount
-- worked out under paragraph (a) is more than $10,000--the lesser of: (i) the amount worked out under paragraph (a); and (ii)
-- the amount of electoral expenditure that is claimed ... and accepted by the Electoral Commission under section 298C." Note:
-- "The dollar amounts specified in paragraphs (2)(a) and (b) are indexed under section 321." Both are INPUTS here; the
-- Commission's acceptance of expenditure is an input amount.
@export How much election funding is payable for me, if any (s 294(2)), in dollars?
GIVEN `my formal first preference votes` IS A NUMBER @desc The formal first preference votes given for you
      `the indexed rate per vote`         IS A NUMBER @desc The s 294(2)(a) rate per vote as indexed under s 321 for the election ($5 before indexation)
      `the indexed threshold`             IS A NUMBER @desc The s 294(2)(b) threshold as indexed under s 321 for the election ($10,000 before indexation)
      `my accepted electoral expenditure` IS A NUMBER @desc The electoral expenditure you claimed and the Electoral Commission accepted under s 298C, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much election funding is payable for me` IS
    IF `by the vote` GREATER THAN `the indexed threshold`
    THEN IF `by the vote` AT MOST `my accepted electoral expenditure`
         THEN `by the vote`
         ELSE `my accepted electoral expenditure`
    ELSE `by the vote`
    WHERE
        `by the vote` MEANS `my formal first preference votes` TIMES `the indexed rate per vote`

§§ `287(9), 289(2), 310A -- the candidate return (Part XX Division 5)`

-- s 287(9)(b): a person "ceases to be a candidate in an election at the end of 7 days after the polling day in the election".
@export On what day do I stop being a candidate for the purposes of Part XX (s 287(9)(b))?
GIVEN `the polling day` IS A DATE @desc The polling day, ISO 8601
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day do I stop being a candidate` IS `the polling day` PLUS 7

-- s 287(9)(a): a person "begins to be a candidate in an election on the earliest of" the day of announcing, of nominating, or of
-- a gift or electoral expenditure (or gifts from one source) exceeding the disclosure threshold ($5,000, s 287(1), indexed under
-- s 321AA, so asked as a day, not worked out).
@export On what day did I begin to be a candidate for the purposes of Part XX (s 287(9)(a))?
GIVEN `the day I announced I would be a candidate` IS A DATE @desc The day you announced your candidacy, ISO 8601 (the nomination day if you never announced earlier)
      `the day I nominated`                         IS A DATE @desc The day you nominated, ISO 8601
      `the day gifts or my expenditure first exceeded the disclosure threshold` IS A MAYBE DATE @desc The first day a gift, gifts from one source, or your electoral expenditure for the campaign exceeded the disclosure threshold, if that has happened
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `On what day did I begin to be a candidate` IS
    CONSIDER `the day gifts or my expenditure first exceeded the disclosure threshold`
    WHEN JUST `threshold day` THEN `the earlier day of` `announced or nominated` `threshold day`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `announced or nominated`
    WHERE
        `announced or nominated` MEANS `the earlier day of` `the day I announced I would be a candidate` `the day I nominated`
        GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
              `b` IS A DATE
        GIVETH A DATE
        `the earlier day of` MEANS IF Day `a` AT MOST Day `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- s 310A(1): "The agent of a person who is a candidate for any period of time during a calendar year must provide the Electoral
-- Commission a return". s 289(2): "If the candidate does not appoint an agent, the candidate is taken to be his or her own
-- agent". (4): not if "(a) the candidate is endorsed by a registered political party; and (b) the agent of the registered
-- political party provides a return under section 310 that sets out the information". (5): not if no gift for a federal purpose
-- was received, no electoral expenditure was incurred, and no discretionary benefit was received from the Commonwealth, in the
-- calendar year.
DECLARE `My candidate year` HAS
    `I was a candidate at some time in the calendar year`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am endorsed and my party's return sets out the information`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I received a gift for a federal purpose in the year`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `I incurred electoral expenditure in the year`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I received a discretionary benefit from the Commonwealth in the year` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Must a candidate return be provided for me for the calendar year (s 310A(1), (4), (5))?
GIVEN `the year` IS A `My candidate year` @desc Your candidacy, endorsement, gifts, expenditure and Commonwealth benefits in the calendar year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must a candidate return be provided for me` IF
        `the year`'s `I was a candidate at some time in the calendar year`
    AND NOT `the year`'s `I am endorsed and my party's return sets out the information`
    AND (    `the year`'s `I received a gift for a federal purpose in the year`
         OR  `the year`'s `I incurred electoral expenditure in the year`
         OR  `the year`'s `I received a discretionary benefit from the Commonwealth in the year`)

-- s 289(1), (2): the candidate may appoint an agent; if not, the candidate is his or her own agent, and so carries s 310A(1).
@export Must I provide the candidate return myself (ss 289(2), 310A(1))?
GIVEN `the year`               IS A `My candidate year` @desc Your candidacy in the calendar year
      `I appointed an agent`   IS A BOOLEAN             @desc Whether you appointed someone as your agent for the election
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I provide the candidate return myself` IF
        `Must a candidate return be provided for me` `the year`
    AND NOT `I appointed an agent`

-- s 310A(2): the return must "be provided to the Electoral Commission within 8 weeks of the end of the calendar year". Read as
-- 56 days after 31 December (INFERENCE on the count).
@export By when must the candidate return for a calendar year be provided (s 310A(2))?
GIVEN `the calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year in which you were a candidate, e.g. 2040
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the candidate return be provided` IS Date 31 12 `the calendar year` PLUS 56

-- s 310A(1), civil penalty: "The higher of the following: (a) 120 penalty units; (b) if an amount is not disclosed ... and there
-- is sufficient evidence for the court to determine the amount, or an estimate of the amount, not disclosed--3 times that
-- amount." The value of a penalty unit is an INPUT.
@export What is the most that can be ordered for not providing the candidate return (s 310A(1) civil penalty), in dollars?
GIVEN `the value of a penalty unit` IS A NUMBER @desc The dollar value of one Commonwealth penalty unit (Crimes Act 1914 s 4AA)
      `the amount not disclosed`    IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the court finds or estimates was not disclosed, in dollars (0 if none can be determined)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most that can be ordered for no candidate return` IS
    IF 120 TIMES `the value of a penalty unit` AT LEAST 3 TIMES `the amount not disclosed`
    THEN 120 TIMES `the value of a penalty unit`
    ELSE 3 TIMES `the amount not disclosed`
